WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.279
Module Five, Lesson One: reasoning strategies.

2
00:00:03.609 --> 00:00:07.463
Six techniques, each with a price tag and a phrase that gives it away.

3
00:00:08.263 --> 00:00:11.755
Picture an HR help bot at a company of two thousand people.

4
00:00:12.085 --> 00:00:15.811
To make it smarter, the team sends every question through Tree of Thoughts.

5
00:00:16.611 --> 00:00:19.867
Now a question about vacation days takes thirty seconds.

6
00:00:20.197 --> 00:00:23.113
The bill grows tenfold, and the answers are no better.

7
00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:28.087
Chain of thought is the cheapest: one linear reasoning path before the answer.

8
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:32.889
It costs one to two times the baseline, and the phrase is: think step by step.

9
00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:37.693
Self-consistency samples several chains and takes a majority vote.

10
00:00:38.023 --> 00:00:40.725
Sample five chains, and you pay five times.

11
00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:45.891
Tree of Thoughts branches, scores partial solutions, searches, and backtracks.

12
00:00:46.221 --> 00:00:50.117
At five to twenty times the baseline, it is the priciest of the six.

13
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:55.561
It fits only when exploring branches helps, and the model can score partial states.

14
00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:58.330
Without that score there is nothing to search on,

15
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.107
so never use it for a quick lookup.

16
00:01:00.907 --> 00:01:03.304
Chain of Verification drafts an answer,

17
00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:06.127
asks itself checking questions, then revises.

18
00:01:06.457 --> 00:01:09.841
It costs three to four times, and it targets factual errors.

19
00:01:10.641 --> 00:01:15.071
Reflexion writes a self-critique after a failure and keeps it for the next attempt.

20
00:01:15.401 --> 00:01:18.786
Debate has agents argue positions while a judge decides.

21
00:01:19.586 --> 00:01:22.245
Modern reasoning models already think internally.

22
00:01:22.575 --> 00:01:25.453
Adding a step by step prompt duplicates that work,

23
00:01:25.503 --> 00:01:28.029
so a simple lookup needs no scaffold at all.

24
00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:32.214
Treat reasoning effort as a routed decision, not a constant.

25
00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:36.658
Easy requests get a direct answer, medium ones get chain of thought,

26
00:01:36.708 --> 00:01:39.107
and only hard ones get voting or search.

27
00:01:39.907 --> 00:01:43.228
A confidence estimate or a small classifier picks the lane.

28
00:01:43.558 --> 00:01:46.559
It is the same routing idea used to choose models.

29
00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:50.850
And the HR bot still gets the new parental leave policy wrong.

30
00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.546
Reasoning cannot invent a fact the model never had, so the fix is retrieval.

31
00:01:56.346 --> 00:01:58.951
On the exam, match the phrase to the technique,

32
00:01:59.001 --> 00:02:02.397
and distrust expensive reasoning offered for a knowledge gap.

33
00:02:02.727 --> 00:02:05.429
The full cost table is waiting in the lesson below.
